answer:  First, we need to determine how much sauce Freda made from the 32 ounces of tomatoes. Since the tomatoes lose half their volume when cooked, the original volume of the tomatoes must be twice the volume of the sauce.

So, the original volume of the tomatoes is:
\[ 32 \text{ ounces} \times 2 = 64 \text{ ounces} \]

Next, we know that each 16-ounce can of tomatoes contains 3 tomatoes. To find out how many 16-ounce cans Freda used, we divide the total volume of the tomatoes by the volume of each can:
\[ \frac{64 \text{ ounces}}{16 \text{ ounces/can}} = 4 \text{ cans} \]

Since each can contains 3 tomatoes, the total number of tomatoes used is:
\[ 4 \text{ cans} \times 3 \text{ tomatoes/can} = 12 \text{ tomatoes} \]

Therefore, Freda used 12 tomatoes.
